# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cache
#
# The analysis caches ARE committed, deliberately. A cold warm_cache run is
# 40+ minutes of HTTP reads, and CropScape -- which CDL comes from -- is
# regularly slow or down, so a developer who clones on a bad day cannot warm
# the library at all. Shipping these makes the repo clone-and-run.
#
# Note the patterns exclude cache CONTENTS, not the directory: git will not
# re-include a file underneath an excluded directory, so `cache/` followed by
# a negation would not work. The `**/` prefix matters too: a pattern that
# contains a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so plain
# `cache/scenes_*` would only match a cache at the repo root and would quietly
# miss r/cache and python/cache.
#
# What is excluded and why:
#   scenes_*  STAC catalogue results. Keyed on the literal end date, so the
#             current-year queries mint a new entry every day they run --
#             committing them would grow history indefinitely. Each one costs
#             about 9 seconds to rebuild.
**/cache/scenes_*

# Figures and derived exports, except the two that are runtime dependencies:
#   demo_library*.csv   read by app.R for the crop labels on the field tiles
#   r_reference/        read by python/compare_with_r.py for the parity check
**/outputs/*
!**/outputs/demo_library.csv
!**/outputs/demo_library_python.csv
!**/outputs/r_reference/
# Kept because the README argues from it: the four-way palette comparison
# behind "Colouring the three fractions". The other figures in outputs/ are
# regenerable demo output and stay ignored.
!**/outputs/18_palette_options.png
# Kept for the same reason: the two-year cover cycle the soil armor section
# argues from, and the basis for the future-work notes there.
!**/outputs/19_two_year_cover.png
# And the cotton pair, which is the clearest case in the library for why the
# off-season is the part worth measuring.
!**/outputs/20_cotton_two_years.png
**/results/

# R
*.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
.Rdata
.RData

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Rasters fetched or written during a run
*.tif

# Validation run logs -- noise, the CSVs are the record
validation/*.log

# Local bulk CDL store. Normally lives outside the repo (~/geodata/cdl);
# this is a backstop for anyone who points CDL_DIR inside it.
geodata/
**/geodata/
*_30m_cdls.tif
*_30m_cdls.zip
*.tif.ovr

# ...but the pre-clipped CDL for the demo library MUST ship: it is what makes
# the deployed Shiny app independent of CropScape. 88 files, 1.7 MB.
# The parent directory is not excluded, so this negation takes effect.
!r/cdl_clips/*.tif

# Intermediate HTML from build_methods_pdf.py (use --keep-html to inspect)
pitch/_methods.html
METHODS.html

# Project-level test inputs: grower-identifying data, deliberately not committed.
# The Fieldprint payloads carry grower email addresses, farm names and yields,
# and the boundaries are precise farm locations. The derived results are keyed
# by a geometry hash instead, so the analysis is reviewable without them.
# Drop the payload archive back in and re-run extract_flash.py to reproduce.
project-level-tests/*/Fieldprint-payloads/
project-level-tests/*/boundaries/
project-level-tests/*/fields.csv
project-level-tests/*/run.log
project-level-tests/*/_flash_slides.html
project-level-tests/4d-farm/boundaries/

# The 4D farm vendor export: 120 MB of yield monitor, soil moisture, as-applied
# and electrical-conductivity files, same grower-data reasoning as above. Some
# of its paths also exceed the Windows path limit, so git cannot index them at
# all. extract_4d_ancillary.py reduces it to ancillary_summary.csv, which is
# what the workbook was built from and is committed.
project-level-tests/4d-farm/ancillary data/

# The alfalfa report pack: a Shiny export carrying a precise farm boundary,
# same grower-data reasoning as the Fieldprint payloads above. The derived
# cuttings.csv, the figures and the deck are committed; drop the pack back
# into alfalfa-nm/pack/ to reproduce them.
project-level-tests/alfalfa-nm/pack/
